            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac Tamponade Diagnosed by Point-of-Care Ultrasound.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>132-134</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/PEC.0000000000001024</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case involving a 12-year-old boy who presented to the emergency department and was diagnosed with a pericardial effusion with tamponade physiology by point-of-care ultrasound. The diagnosis resulted in prompt treatment and definitive therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
